---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { withBase } from "../lib/url";
import meet from "../../config/meet.json";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About & Disclaimer"
  description="Road to Zones is an independent, unofficial resource. It is not Arizona Swimming or USA Swimming, and it does not select teams."
>
  <h1 class="page-title">About this site</h1>
  <p class="page-subtitle">
    Road to Zones exists for one reason: Arizona has more Zones-eligible 14&amp;U swimmers than it
    sends. This site tries to make that gap visible so fewer families miss the chance.
  </p>

  <div class="card callout callout-warn">
    <h2 class="card-heading">Please read this part</h2>
    <ul class="tight-list">
      <li>
        This is an <strong>independent, unofficial</strong> resource. It is
        <strong>not affiliated with Arizona Swimming (AZSI), USA Swimming, or the Western Zone</strong>,
        and it does not speak for any of them.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Eligibility shown here is not selection.</strong> Meeting a AAA standard does not put a
        swimmer on a team. Only the LSC selects the Zone team, by its own process.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Always confirm with your club coach.</strong> If this site and your coach disagree,
        your coach is right.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2 class="card-heading">What the site does and doesn't know</h2>
    <p>
      The <a href={withBase("/calculator")}>eligibility calculator</a> compares a time you type in
      against the published AAA time standards. It runs entirely in your browser — nothing you enter
      is sent anywhere, stored, or logged.
    </p>
    <p>
      Time standards come from the 2025–2028 USA Swimming National Age Group Motivational Standards
      ("AAA", combined age group), as published in the Western Zone Age Group Championships standards
      document. They're reproduced here for reference; the official documents govern.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-bottom:0">
      <strong>Times are never converted between courses.</strong> A long course time is only ever
      compared against the long course standard, short course meters against short course meters, and
      yards against yards. Zones does not accept converted times, so neither does this site.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2 class="card-heading">Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      This site collects <strong>no birthdates</strong> — not from you, not from anywhere else. The
      calculator asks for an age only to pick the right standards table, and that value never leaves
      your device.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-bottom:0">
      There are no accounts, no trackers, and no analytics on this site.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2 class="card-heading">Target meet</h2>
    <p>
      Everything on this site is calculated against <strong>{meet.meetName}</strong>.
    </p>
    <ul class="tight-list">
      <li>Location: <strong>{meet.location}</strong></li>
      <li>First day of competition: <strong>{meet.firstDayOfCompetition}</strong></li>
      <li>Entry deadline: <strong>{meet.entryDeadline}</strong></li>
    </ul>
    <p class="note" style="margin-bottom:0">
      ⚠️ The {meet.targetYear} dates and host city have <strong>not been announced yet</strong>. The
      values above are placeholders so the math has something to work with, and they will change.
      Don't book flights based on this page.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2 class="card-heading">Found a mistake?</h2>
    <p style="margin-bottom:0">
      Corrections are genuinely welcome — especially on the time standards, where a typo could tell a
      swimmer the wrong thing. Reporting links will be added here shortly.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
